clear_fields.description:
Fields to empty — empty values are otherwise ignored. Allowed: description;
args, env_vars_schema, cli_args_mapping (removed from the stored local config, the rest is kept);
env_vars, auth_config (both are the one stored credentials object — clearing either removes
all stored credentials). The result lists them under "cleared".

tools.description:
Check a run started with start_run (or any session of yours) and read its answer when done.

Returns the platform's processing fields plus "status":
  "running"   — still working (current_agent, elapsed_seconds tell you where it is); poll again;
  "completed" — the newest turn is an assistant reply; "result" holds it (include_result=True);
  "timed_out" — the status stopped reporting it after 120 minutes; the run itself may still be going;
  "pending"   — the session exists but nothing has been said yet; poll again;
  "no_reply"  — not running, and the newest message is the user's: the run ended without an answer;
  "not_found" — no such session for this key (wrong id, or another user's session).
Right after start_run on a session that already had turns, the previous answer can show as
"completed" until the new run begins — trust "completed" once you have seen "running".

schedule_config.description:
REQUIRED — the backend rejects the request with 400 when it is missing, so the
"daily" default above is not usable on its own. Times are KST. Shape per type:
daily: {"time": "09:00"}
weekly: {"time": "09:00", "weekdays": [0,1,2,3,4]}  (0=Monday)
monthly: {"day": 1, "time": "09:00"}
every_minutes: {"interval": 30}
every_hours: {"interval": 6}
once: {"run_at": "2025-12-01T09:00:00"}

tools.description:
One call for the whole automatic pipeline: add a web page (`url`) OR documents (`files`, base64) to Knowledge, then poll the source until
it is `ready` (or failed) and return its final state. Bounded: `timeout_s` ≤ 120 — larger ingests return {status: "timeout", source_id}
and should be followed with knowledge_source. Reading, organizing, map/ontology and graph building need no further calls.

Turn a quality flag that measured rollouts switched on for everyone off for this organization only (opt_out=true),
or follow the platform default again (opt_out=false). Only flags marked org_can_opt_out in get_effective_feature_flags;
security, audit and billing flags cannot be changed here. Ask the user first.
